<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>netstandard2.1;net8.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <!-- Ship the XML documentation alongside the assembly, so a consumer of the package gets the
         doc comments as IntelliSense. This project is clean of CS1591, so a public member added
         without one now warns. Set per project rather than in Directory.Build.props, which is
         imported before IsPackable is known, or Directory.Build.targets, which is
         imported after the SDK has already derived DocumentationFile from it. -->
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <Description>ImageSharp 2.1 imaging and font backend for PdfPinata.

Provides ImageSharpImageSource, ImageSharpFontResolver and ImageSharpGlyphOutlineProvider, built against SixLabors.ImageSharp 2.1.x and SixLabors.Fonts 1.0.1, the last releases under the Apache-2.0 licence. ImageSharp 2.1.x is end of life and has five security advisories that will never be fixed.

Use PdfPinata.ImageSharp4 instead, unless you target Unity (netstandard2.1) or must keep your dependencies under Apache-2.0. Both packages have the same types in the same namespaces, so switching between them is a change to the project file only.</Description>
    <summary>ImageSharp backend for PdfPinata</summary>
    <IsTrimmable>true</IsTrimmable>
    <EnableTrimAnalyzer>true</EnableTrimAnalyzer>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- ImageSharp 3.0 is not binary compatible with 2.1.x: the Load(..., out IImageFormat)
         overloads were removed and every encoder property changed from set to init, which
         alters the setter signature. Code compiled here against 2.1.x throws
         MissingMethodException if the consumer's graph unifies ImageSharp to 3.x, so the
         upper bound turns that into a restore-time version conflict instead. See #348. -->
    <PackageReference Include="SixLabors.ImageSharp" Version="[2.1.13,3.0.0)" />
    <PackageReference Include="SixLabors.Fonts" Version="1.0.1" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\PdfPinata\PdfPinata.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    The backend's source lives in src/ImageSharpBackend, not here, because two packages compile it:
    this one against ImageSharp 2.1.x and PdfPinata.ImageSharp4 against 4.x. The calls that differ
    between the two majors sit behind the IMAGESHARP4 constant, which this project does not define.
    One copy of each file, so a fix reaches both packages. See #305.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Include="..\ImageSharpBackend\*.cs" Link="%(Filename)%(Extension)" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
